> Blue opened his button eyes and looked around the lab.
> 
> “Friend?” he rumbled.
> 
> Mr. Red was thrilled. “Yes! You’re a friend! A Rainbow Friend!”
> 
> But Blue didn’t understand much yet. He only knew one thing:
> 
> He didn’t want to be alone.
> 
> So whenever he saw people, he lumbered after them, hoping they would stay and play. But Blue was huge, and his footsteps shook the floor, and everyone got scared and ran away.
> 
> That made Blue sad.
> 
> And when Blue got sad, he chased even harder.
> 
> ## Green
> 
> Green came next.
> 
> Green was long and wiggly, with giant googly eyes…
> 
> …except Green couldn’t actually see very well at all.
> 
> He moved with his hands stretched out, feeling walls, doors, and footsteps through the floor. Green didn’t chase because he was mean.
> 
> He chased because he was **searching**.
> 
> He wanted to find where he belonged.
> 
> Sometimes he heard people whispering and thought,
> “Oh! Maybe those are my friends!”
> 
> But when he reached for them, they screamed and ran.
> 
> That made Green confused.
> 
> ## Orange
> 
> Orange was fast.
> 
> Very fast.
> 
> He was made from the part of the rainbow that never wanted to sit still. Orange zoomed through tunnels and hallways like a flash of fire.
> 
